Circular route from the car park in front of Sant Serní del Grau through: 
- Coll de la Creu de Canalda (0.9 km) 
- Tossal de Vall-llonga (2.5 km) 
- Collet del Santuari (4.0 km) 
- Viacrucis Viewpoint (4.2 km) 
- Sant Pere Màrtir (4.4 km) 
- Mola de Lord (4.5 km) 
- Lord''s Sanctuary (4.8 km) 
- Mirador de la Trona (5.6 km) 
- Hermitage of Sant Jaume (6.5 km) 
- Mirador Josep Cases (6.6 km) 
- Sant Isidre Fountain (7.9 km) 
- Hermitage of Sant Serní del Grau (8.9 km) 
- Roc Foradat tunnel (9.1 km) 
- Vilamantells Cemetery (10.1 km) 
- Sant Serní del Grau (10.1 km) 
 
 
START OF THE WALK. 
 We start today''s walk in front of the picnic area Font de Sant Serní, Vilamantells (Sant Llorenç de Morunys - Solsonès). 
 The car park is located on the right side of the path of the Lord''s Sanctuary, in front of the hermitage of Sant Serní del Grau. It is reached by a road that leaves the LV-4241 road (from Sant Llorenç de Morunys to Port del Comte). 
 
 We go towards the Santuari del Lord and Roc Foradat (Coll de la Creu de Canalda), later we leave the path, we continue to the right along the GR-7 path, it is also very well marked by the indicators, after the Roc Foradat we leave the GR 7 and continue to the left until we find the asphalted path of the Sanctuary of the Lord, we follow it a little and we go to the left leaving the path of Tossal As we go up and until we reach the other side of the hill we enjoy wonderful panoramic views, continue the path again find the Lord''s Sanctuary Path, we follow it and soon we reach the Santuari pass. 
Here begins the Way of the Cross (Latin expression meaning "Camí de la Creu"). At the time of the Via Crucis they are called "stations" and are traditionally 14 listed. 
We will go up in zigzag until we reach the hill, when we arrive and in the first place there is the hermitage dedicated to Sant Pere Màrtir, we continue to reach the Mola de Lord and then we go to the Sanctuary of Lord. 
 After visiting the Sanctuary we continue the walk towards the hermitage of Sant Jaume, but before we go to the right to visit the Mirador de la Trona with magnificent panoramic views of the Llossa del Cavall reservoir, which we will enjoy in a good stretch of the route. We return back along the path to continue the previous path, we pass through the hermitage of Sant Jaume and then we find the Mirador Josep Cases. We continue down the path and continue to the left bordering under the Tossal de la Mola de Lord until we reach the Collet del Santuari (the route is very well indicated). 
 From here we start the return along the Camí del Santuari (without leaving the path we will reach the starting point of the walk), later there is the Font de Sant Isidre and then the tunnel excavated in the rock, from here there is approximately a km to reach the starting point of the walk, where we visit Sant Serní del Grau. 
 
PANORAMIC VIEWS OF THE ROUTE: 
 Serra del Port del Comte, Tossal del Codó, Serrat de Sòbol con la Paret de l’Embut de Vilamala y la Balma del Fornó, Tossal de Vall-Llonga, Cingles de les Valls, Serrat de la Creueta, embalse de la Llosa del Cavall, la Serra de Busa, Els Llengots y la Serra dels Bastets, La Serra de Guixers con la Roca de Guixers, Serrat de Pratformiu y la Serra Del Verd, Serra d’Ensija i Rasos de Peguera,... 
 
END OF A MAGNIFICENT WALK!!! 
 
